# Golden fixtures are byte-compared against encoder output in tests
# (`assert_eq!(format!("{encoded}\n"), include_str!(...))`). The canonical
# bytes are what JSON.stringify produced — LF line endings — so these paths
# must materialize with LF on every OS. Without this, core.autocrlf rewrites
# them to CRLF on Windows checkouts: parsing still succeeds but the blob's
# trailing byte differs, so the round-trip assertions fail on Windows only.
fixtures/** text eol=lf
crates/memoria-model/fixtures/** text eol=lf
crates/memoria-model/src/obsidian/tests/golden/** text eol=lf
# Editor fixtures: byte-exact too; crlf.md must keep its CRLF on every OS.
crates/memoria-editor-core/tests/fixtures/*.md text eol=lf
crates/memoria-editor-core/tests/fixtures/crlf.md -text

# Binary payloads must never be EOL-normalized.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
